[size=5][b]Changelog[/b][/size]

[size=4][color=#ffd700][b]v1.1.0 (DnD 5.5e Beyond Compatibility & Comprehensive Tooltips)[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Terminology Standardization (Focus & Channel):[/b]
[list]
[*]Streamlined and standardized all terminology across the entire mod, Lua engine, and documentation to strictly use [b]Focus[/b] (buff layer) and [b]Channel[/b] (combat layer). Removed legacy and ambiguous references to "conduit".
[/list]
[*][b]100% Comprehensive In-Game Tooltip Coverage:[/b]
[list]
[*]Over 480+ in-game spell cards, upcasts (levels 2–6), scrolls, racial abilities (e.g. Drow [i]Faerie Fire[/i]), and applied status tooltips now feature dedicated [b]Focus[/b] and [b]Channel[/b] mechanic descriptions.
[*]Bumped internal localization version numbers to [b]version="10"[/b], guaranteeing mod descriptions always override base game strings regardless of load order.
[/list]
[*][b]DnD 5.5e All-In-One BEYOND Compatibility:[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Illrigger:[/b] Full Combat Channeling for all subclasses ([i]Sanguine Knight[/i], [i]Hellspeaker[/i], [i]Painkiller[/i], [i]Shadowmaster[/i], [i]Architect of Ruin[/i]). Whitelisted all Seals, Interdicts, Hell abilities, and Blood Price.
[*][b]Monster Hunter:[/b] Full Combat Channeling for [i]Carver Guild[/i], [i]Devourer Guild[/i], and [i]Occultist Guild[/i]. Whitelisted all Mutations and Hunting Tactics.
[*][b]Artificer:[/b] Combat Channeling for martial gish subclasses ([i]Battle Smith[/i], [i]Armorer[/i]). Whitelisted Experimental Elixirs, Armor Models, and Defensive Field.
[*][b]Gunslinger:[/b] Combat Channeling for the [i]Spellslinger[/i] gun gish subclass.
[*][b]New Subclasses Across Existing Classes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Fighter: [i]Rune Knight[/i], [i]Psi Warrior[/i], [i]Arcane Archer[/i], [i]Cavalier[/i], [i]Banneret[/i], [i]Viking[/i].
[*]Rogue: [i]Soulknife[/i], [i]Blade of Radiance[/i], [i]Arachnoid Stalker[/i].
[*]Bard: [i]College of Dance[/i], [i]College of Choreography[/i].
[*]Cleric: [i]Forge Domain[/i], [i]Twilight Domain[/i], [i]Dragon Domain[/i].
[*]Wizard & Warlock: [i]Bladesinger[/i] (Bladesinging School) and [i]Hexblade[/i].
[*]Monk, Paladin, Ranger: All 2024 subclasses ([i]Mercy[/i], [i]Kensei[/i], [i]Sun Soul[/i], [i]Mystic Arts[/i], [i]Glory[/i], [i]Noble Genie[/i], [i]Conquest[/i], [i]Watchers[/i], [i]Fey Wanderer[/i], [i]Winter Walker[/i], [i]Hollow Warden[/i]) fully integrated.
[/list]
[*][b]38 Custom/Revised Concentration Spells:[/b] Audited, categorized, and annotated all 2024 concentration spells ([i]Holy Weapon[/i], [i]Spellfire Storm[/i], [i]Dragon's Breath[/i], [i]Summon Celestial[/i], [i]Summon Dragon[/i], [i]Void Strike[/i], [i]Murmurs of Doom[/i], etc.).
[/list]
[*][b]Spell Weaving (Cantrips, Bonus Actions & Quickened Metamagic):[/b]
[list]
[*][b]All Cantrips (Level 0):[/b] Pure casters now have an active combat loop every turn! All cantrips ([i]Fire Bolt[/i], [i]Ray of Frost[/i], [i]Eldritch Blast[/i], [i]Sacred Flame[/i], [i]Acid Splash[/i], [i]Shocking Grasp[/i], etc.) are recognized as reflexive magic and can be cast freely without breaking an active Channel.
[*][b]Native Bonus Action Spells:[/b] Spells requiring only a Bonus Action ([i]Misty Step[/i], [i]Healing Word[/i], [i]Mass Healing Word[/i], [i]Spiritual Weapon[/i], [i]Sanctuary[/i]) can now be cast without breaking Channel, enabling fluid tactical repositioning and emergency triage.
[*][b]Sorcerer Quickened Spell Metamagic:[/b] Quickening a standard-action leveled spell converts it to a bonus action weave, allowing Sorcerers to spend Sorcery Points to cast leveled spells without dropping their active Channel stance.
[*][b]Action Leveled Spells:[/b] Casting standard-action leveled spells (Level 1+) or offensive reactions ([i]Counterspell[/i], [i]Hellish Rebuke[/i]) continues to demand total mental concentration and breaks active Channel stances.
[/list]
[*][b]Engine & Packaging Stability (Patch 7 / Patch 8+):[/b]
[list]
[*]Resolved a launch crash ([i]0xC0000005[/i] in [i]bg3_dx11.exe[/i]) caused by raw XML linebreaks creating text DOM nodes without attributes in Larian's localization parser.
[*]Re-architected localization pipeline into clean single-line entries with [i]&#10;[/i] line breaks and compiled binary [i].loca[/i].
[*]Removed duplicate package namespace directories and automated loose file cleanup on deployment.
[/list]
[/list]

[size=4][color=#ffd700][b]v1.0.5[/b][/color][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Haste Dual Duration & Intelligent Lethargy System:[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Self-Cast (Indefinite):[/b] Indefinite Channel spell with unlimited duration.
[*][b]Ally-Cast (10 Rounds):[/b] Standard tactical duration of 10 rounds (60 seconds) when cast on party members, companions, or summons.
[*][b]Safe Release (No Lethargy):[/b] Voluntarily ending [i]Haste[/i]—by clicking portrait "X", casting non-whitelisted spells or offensive reactions, swapping Channel spells, or letting the 10 rounds expire naturally on an ally—safely releases the recipient with zero Lethargy ([i]"Haste Ended (Safe Release)"[/i]).
[*][b]Involuntary Disruption (Inflicts Lethargy):[/b] Breaking your Channel involuntarily via damage, environmental surfaces, or hard crowd control ([i]Hold Person[/i], [i]Sleep[/i], [i]Hypnotic Pattern[/i], [i]Banishment[/i], [i]Stun[/i], [i]Paralyze[/i]) inflicts 1 turn of Lethargy ([i]"Lethargic! (Damage/Incapacitated Disruption)"[/i]).
[*][b]Sorcerer Twinned Haste Support:[/b] Twinning Haste grants the caster an indefinite buff while the ally receives the 10-round buff. When the ally's duration expires, the ally releases safely without Lethargy, leaving the caster's Haste intact.
[*][b]In-Game Tooltips:[/b] Fully updated spell card and status tooltips reflecting dual-duration and intelligent lethargy rules.
[/list]
[*][b]Gish Reaction Defensives & Melee Cantrips:[/b]
[list]
[*]Combat Channelers and characters with [i]War Caster[/i] (enabling build-your-own gish setups on pure Sorcerers or Wizards) can cast personal reaction defensives ([i]Shield[/i], [i]Absorb Elements[/i]) and melee spell cantrips ([i]Green-Flame Blade[/i], [i]Booming Blade[/i], [i]Vengeful Blade[/i]) without breaking active Channel spells.
[*]Offensive counter-magic ([i]Counterspell[/i]) and retaliatory damage reactions ([i]Hellish Rebuke[/i]) demand full casting focus and continue to break active Channel spells for all casters.
[/list]
[*][b]Gish Combat Stances & Class Forms:[/b]
[list]
[*]Activating martial class stances and disciplines ([i]Bladesong[/i], [i]Symbiotic Entity[/i], [i]Bind Pact Weapon[/i], [i]Hexblade's Curse[/i], [i]Weapon Bond[/i], Monk Ki maneuvers/stances, Bardic [i]Blade Flourishes[/i], and martial [i]Channel Divinities[/i]) never breaks an active Channel spell.
[/list]
[*][b]Loss of Control & Hard CC:[/b]
[list]
[*]Hard incapacitation conditions ([i]Stunned[/i], [i]Paralyzed[/i], [i]Sleeping[/i], [i]Incapacitated[/i], [i]Banished[/i]) reliably sever both Focus and Channel and trigger full disruption penalties.
[/list]
[/list]

[size=4][b]v1.0.4[/b][/size]
